# Organization Source

Organization is presented as a universal mental model—a conceptual tool for navigating complex situations through pattern and relationship recognition. It draws on systems thinking from Peter M. Senge's *The Fifth Discipline* and leadership culture principles from Simon Sinek's *Leaders Eat Last*.

This source provides a high-level definition but minimal elaboration, positioning organization as a framework distinct from management or planning, though related to both.
